WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.934 --> 00:00:24.041
"Wow, there are a lot of people here," Cole said.

2
00:00:24.042 --> 00:00:29.243
"I know." Maggie sounded happy. "We might need to make more lemonade."

3
00:00:29.244 --> 00:00:30.891
Henry smiled.

4
00:00:30.892 --> 00:00:36.795
It had been Maggie's idea to set up their lemonade stand at the park for Belltown Arts Day.

5
00:00:36.796 --> 00:00:39.669
She'd thought they would make lots of money.

6
00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:44.717
And it looked like she was right. The stand had been busy all morning long.

7
00:00:44.718 --> 00:00:48.518
Belltown Arts Day was a popular tradition in Belltown.

8
00:00:48.519 --> 00:00:53.279
It was a whole day of art, music, and crafts for all ages.

9
00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:56.395
There was a crafts fair at one end of the park.

10
00:00:56.396 --> 00:01:03.003
People had set up booths there to display crafts like glassblowing and basket weaving.

11
00:01:03.004 --> 00:01:08.636
At the other end of the park, right in front of the Belltown Museum of Art, was an art show.

12
00:01:08.637 --> 00:01:13.527
Anyone could enter a painting, sculpture, or other piece of art in the show.

13
00:01:13.528 --> 00:01:18.351
That afternoon a committee of experts was going to judge all the pieces.

14
00:01:18.352 --> 00:01:23.838
The pieces that won first place would be displayed in the museum for the rest of the year.

15
00:01:23.839 --> 00:01:29.669
The bandstand in the middle of the park featured a full schedule of musical acts and dance groups.

16
00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:33.196
Right now a fiddler was playing a lively tune.

17
00:01:33.197 --> 00:01:38.024
Henry, Maggie, and Cole had set up the lemonade stand near the bandstand.

18
00:01:38.025 --> 00:01:40.604
Cole tapped his foot along with the music.

19
00:01:40.605 --> 00:01:43.611
"Here come some more customers," he said.

20
00:01:43.612 --> 00:01:49.620
For the next few minutes, The Lemonade Detectives stayed busy pouring lemonade and collecting money.

21
00:01:49.621 --> 00:01:53.943
When the last customer wandered off, Henry turned to his friends.

22
00:01:53.944 --> 00:01:56.704
"We should look for Nathan," he said.

23
00:01:56.705 --> 00:02:00.298
"I want to see his painting before the judging starts."

24
00:02:00.299 --> 00:02:04.832
"Me too," Cole agreed. "I heard it's really good."

25
00:02:04.833 --> 00:02:07.555
Their friend Nathan was a talented artist.

26
00:02:07.556 --> 00:02:10.692
This was his first year entering the art show.

27
00:02:10.693 --> 00:02:14.366
He was competing in the Age 12 and Under category.

28
00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:18.156
The other two categories were for teenagers and adults.

29
00:02:18.157 --> 00:02:23.229
Maggie looked around. "I guess we can take a short break," she said.

30
00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:25.541
"I want to see Nathan's painting too.

31
00:02:25.542 --> 00:02:29.476
His little sister, Nora, can't stop talking about it."

32
00:02:29.477 --> 00:02:34.543
Cole laughed. "Nora can never stop talking!" he joked.

33
00:02:34.544 --> 00:02:38.021
"She talks more than any other little kid I know."

34
00:02:38.022 --> 00:02:41.389
The Lemonade Detectives set out a Closed sign.

35
00:02:41.390 --> 00:02:44.966
Then they headed across the crowded park to the art show.

36
00:02:44.967 --> 00:02:48.418
They found Nathan standing in front of his painting.

37
00:02:48.419 --> 00:02:51.634
Nora was sitting on the ground, playing with a doll.

38
00:02:51.635 --> 00:02:54.981
Nathan's mom was chatting with a friend nearby.

39
00:02:54.982 --> 00:02:59.438
Nathan was talking to a red-haired boy named Patrick and his parents.

40
00:02:59.439 --> 00:03:03.050
Patrick was in the grade below Henry, Cole, and Nathan.

41
00:03:03.051 --> 00:03:08.455
"Hi, Patrick," Henry greeted him. "Did you enter the art show too?"

42
00:03:08.456 --> 00:03:12.645
"Of course," Patrick said. "I enter the show every year.

43
00:03:12.646 --> 00:03:15.602
My painting came in third place last year."

44
00:03:15.603 --> 00:03:21.841
"Wow." Nathan sounded impressed. "I'd be thrilled to come in third place."

45
00:03:21.842 --> 00:03:26.563
Patrick looked at Nathan's painting. Henry looked closely too.

46
00:03:26.564 --> 00:03:30.997
Nathan had painted a very good watercolor of a calico cat.

47
00:03:30.998 --> 00:03:36.001
"I'm sorry to say this, Nathan, but you probably won't win," Patrick declared.

48
00:03:36.002 --> 00:03:39.585
"Art judges don't usually like pictures of animals."

49
00:03:39.586 --> 00:03:44.657
Maggie frowned. "I think Nathan's cat painting is amazing!"

50
00:03:44.658 --> 00:03:49.223
Nora looked up. "Are you talking about my kitty?"

51
00:03:49.224 --> 00:03:53.015
"Your kitty?" Henry looked at the painting again.

52
00:03:53.016 --> 00:03:56.743
"Oh, I get it. It's a painting of Patches."

53
00:03:56.744 --> 00:03:59.443
That was the name of Nora's pet cat.

54
00:03:59.444 --> 00:04:03.968
"You should try painting a landscape next year, Nathan," Patrick went on.

55
00:04:03.969 --> 00:04:08.633
"That's what I did. My art teacher thinks I'll win first place this year."

56
00:04:08.634 --> 00:04:12.021
"We'll see about that," Maggie told Patrick.

57
00:04:12.022 --> 00:04:17.360
"If Patches winds up in the museum and your painting doesn't, you'll regret bragging!"

58
00:04:17.361 --> 00:04:21.570
Nora's eyes widened. "No!" she blurted out.

59
00:04:21.571 --> 00:04:26.593
"Patches can't live in the museum. She lives in my room with me!"

60
00:04:26.594 --> 00:04:29.193
"Don't worry," Henry told her.

61
00:04:29.194 --> 00:04:33.188
"We're not talking about sending Patches away to live in the museum.

62
00:04:33.189 --> 00:04:35.627
Just the painting of her."

63
00:04:35.628 --> 00:04:37.776
Nora still looked upset.

64
00:04:37.777 --> 00:04:42.520
"Nathan said I could hang the painting in my room after the show.

65
00:04:42.521 --> 00:04:46.559
She's my kitty, so I should have the painting!"

66
00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:52.725
"It's okay, Nora," Nathan said. "I'm sure my painting won't win anyway."

67
00:04:52.726 --> 00:04:55.336
Just then another kid ran up to them.

68
00:04:55.337 --> 00:04:59.052
His name was Owen, and he was one of Patrick's friends.

69
00:04:59.053 --> 00:05:04.352
"Guess what, you guys?" Owen said. He stopped to take a big breath.

70
00:05:04.353 --> 00:05:08.397
"I just heard the judges talking about the paintings they liked!"

71
00:05:08.398 --> 00:05:11.727
"Really?" Nathan sounded surprised.

72
00:05:11.728 --> 00:05:15.331
"I thought judging didn't start until two o'clock."

73
00:05:15.332 --> 00:05:21.405
"It doesn't. But I guess they walked through the show and saw some of the artwork already," Owen said.

74
00:05:21.406 --> 00:05:26.401
"All three judges were talking about how good Nathan's cat painting is.

75
00:05:26.402 --> 00:05:30.899
It sounds like he might win!"
